   $q$Mrs. Adeyemi mentions that she has "fed half of them every Saturday for ten years." How does this detail affect the plot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals a long bond with the firefighters, which explains why her request is likely to work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows she plans to sell the bread at the station to make up for her lost sales.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows she is tired of the bakery and wants to close it for good after the storm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that the firefighters owe her money and must let her use their station kitchen.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reveals a long bond with the firefighters, which explains why her request is likely to work.$q$, $q$Years of feeding the firefighters suggest a friendly relationship, which makes her request reasonable, and she returns ten minutes later with permission. The bread is given away under a "Free bread" sign, so she is not selling it.$q$, 'draft', 'e4568690-db85-5b75-a245-49ff9f83b24f')
